message.content:
Storybook fix on branch `feature/SFCC-236_product-card-shared-component` in `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa`, approved by Marcel after he found it live in Storybook: clicking a size chip logs the action but the chip never visually selects.

**Root cause (already diagnosed, don't re-diagnose):** `ZimmSizeChipGroup`/`ZimmProductCard` are correctly controlled components — clicking calls `onSelect`/`onSizeChipSelect` with the new value, but neither component tracks selection itself. Every story except one passes a static `selectedValue`/`selectedSizeChipValue` in plain `args` with `onSelect`/`onSizeChipSelect` as either an auto-mocked no-op or an explicit `fn()` spy (from `storybook/test`) — neither updates the displayed value, so nothing can visually change on click. This is correct, expected behaviour for a controlled component given a non-stateful story; it is not a component bug.

**The fix — apply the SAME existing pattern already used correctly elsewhere in this codebase to exactly two stories, no more:**

1. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmSizeChipGroup/index.stories.tsx` — its `Default` story (currently `args: { values: SIZES, selectedValue: '' }`, around line 25). Follow the exact pattern already used later in this same file for the `KeyboardNavigation` story: a small local component using `useState`, e.g.:
   ```tsx
   const DefaultExample = () => {
     const [selectedValue, setSelectedValue] = useState<string | undefined>('');
     return <ZimmSizeChipGroup values={SIZES} selectedValue={selectedValue} onSelect={setSelectedValue} />;
   };
   export const Default: Story = {
     render: () => <DefaultExample />,
   };
   ```
   Match the real file's existing `KeyboardNavigationExample` naming/structure convention exactly (read it first, it's later in the same file) rather than inventing a different shape. Keep this story's own doc comment (the one-liner above `Default`) — update its wording only if it currently implies the story is a static, non-interactive display (it may need a small edit to reflect that it's now live).

2. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.stories.tsx` — its `Default` story (around lines 76-90, `variation: 'plp'`, currently `sizeChipValues: SIZES, onSizeChipSelect: fn()`, no `selectedSizeChipValue` at all — starts with nothing selected). This story has many more args than just the size-chip pair (id, variation, name, headingLevel, href, images, price, badge, onAddToBag, etc.) — read the full block first. Convert it to a `render` function that wraps `ZimmProductCard` in a small local stateful component, keeping every other arg exactly as it is today and only making `selectedSizeChipValue` genuinely stateful:
   ```tsx
   const DefaultExample = (args: ZimmProductCardProps) => {
     const [selectedSizeChipValue, setSelectedSizeChipValue] = useState<string | undefined>(undefined);
     return (
       <ZimmProductCard
         {...args}
         selectedSizeChipValue={selectedSizeChipValue}
         onSizeChipSelect={(value) => {
           setSelectedSizeChipValue(value);
           args.onSizeChipSelect?.(value); // keep the fn() spy firing so Storybook's Actions panel still logs it
         }}
       />
     );
   };
   ```
   (Adjust the exact type/shape to whatever this file's own types actually are — check `ZimmProductCardProps`'s real import and the real signature of `onSizeChipSelect` before writing this; don't guess the parameter type.) Keep `args` as the source of every other prop (including the `fn()` for `onAddToBag`, which stays untouched) — only `selectedSizeChipValue`/`onSizeChipSelect` become live. This file already renders every story inside a shared decorator providing `MemoryRouter` — check `meta.decorators` and don't duplicate or break that wrapping.

**Do not touch** `WithSelection`, `WithDisabledSize`, `OneSize`, `Wishlist`, `PLPOutOfStock`, `Home`, or any other story in either file — those are deliberately static fixed-state snapshots, not live demos, and should stay exactly as they are. Do not touch `KeyboardNavigation` (already correct, it's the pattern being copied). Do not touch either component's own `index.tsx` logic — this is a stories-only fix.

When done, report the exact diff for both files, confirm `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean, and run `npx vitest run` scoped to any test file that might import these story files (unlikely, but check) plus confirm the two component test files (`zimmSizeChipGroup/index.test.tsx`, `zimmProductCard/index.test.tsx`) still pass unaffected (stories aren't executed by vitest, but confirm nothing else broke). Do not stage, do not commit.

