251	  test('home variation does not accept onRemove (type-only)', () => {
252	    // Assigned to the narrow per-variation intersection, not the `ZimmProductCardProps` union
253	    // alias: TypeScript's excess-property check on a *union* target only flags a property as
254	    // excess when it is unknown to EVERY member, so `onRemove` (valid on the wishlist member)
255	    // would silently pass here even under `variation: 'home'` if assigned to the union type
256	    // directly — confirmed empirically while building this test (an earlier version of this
257	    // exact case, assigned to `ZimmProductCardProps`, produced an "unused @ts-expect-error"
258	    // compile error because of this). The narrow intersection has no such escape hatch: it is a
259	    // plain object type with no `onRemove` key anywhere, so the excess property is genuinely
260	    // unknown and TypeScript reports it.
261	    //
262	    // The directive sits directly above the `onRemove` line, not the `const invalid = {` line
